prompt:
Use Three.js to implement an equestrian show jumping game. The horse automatically runs forward, and the player controls the timing of jumps.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following import map in <head>, and import via ES Modules inside <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/Fox.glb;
(2) Play the running animation on the horse model;

[Track and Obstacles]
(3) A straight track (60m long, visualized with ground stripes);
(4) 6 rail obstacles (BoxGeometry) with different heights (0.5m, 0.8m, 1.0m, 1.2m, 1.0m, 1.5m);
(5) Distribute the obstacles evenly along the track;

[Automatic Running]
(6) The horse automatically runs forward at 6 m/s (no manual forward movement is required);

[Jumping]
(7) Press the Space key to jump;
(8) Jump effect: the horse moves upward along a parabolic trajectory (initial vy=8, g=15);
(9) Good timing: jumping when the distance to a rail is < 1m results in a clear jump and +10 points (the rail remains in place);
(10) Poor timing: if the horse jumps but does not reach sufficient height, it knocks down the rail and receives -5 points (with a rail-falling animation);
(11) No jump: directly colliding with a rail causes the horse to stop and receive -10 points, then continue after 2 seconds;

[HUD Display]
(12) HUD in the upper-left corner:
  - Score (id="score")
  - Number of obstacles cleared (id="cleared")
  - Number of faults (id="faults")
  - Current speed (id="speed")

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
  - modelLoaded: boolean
  - score: number
  - hurdlesCleared: number
  - faults: number
  - speed: number
  - position: number (progress along the track in m)
  - isJumping: boolean

Output a single standalone HTML file.
